## Riverpod rules

### Always use @riverpod (autoDispose by default)
```dart
// CORRECT
@riverpod
class FeatureNotifier extends _$FeatureNotifier { ... }

// WRONG — never use keepAlive: true unless explicitly justified
@Riverpod(keepAlive: true)
@Riverpod(keepAlive: false)  // also wrong — redundant
```

### Notifier pattern
- Extend `AsyncNotifier<T>` via `_$FeatureNotifier`
- `build()` returns `Future<T>` — auto-fetches on first watch
- Use `ref.mounted` guard after every `await`
- Optimistic updates: save previous state, update optimistically, rollback on exception

```dart
Future<void> addEntry(Entry entry) async {
  final previous = state;
  state = AsyncData([...state.value ?? [], entry]);
  try {
    final saved = await _repository.addEntry(entry);
    state = AsyncData([...state.value!..remove(entry), saved]);
  } catch (e) {
    state = previous;
    rethrow;
  }
}
```

### Repository provider
- Returns the interface, not the concrete class
```dart
@riverpod
IFeatureRepository featureRepository(Ref ref) {
  final base = ref.watch(wgerBaseProvider);
  final api = FeatureApiService(base);
  return FeatureRepository(api);
}
```

