## Migration checklist — legacy provider → Clean Architecture

When migrating lib/providers/<feature>.dart to lib/features/<feature>/:

- [ ] Create folder structure mirroring lib/features/body_weight/
- [ ] Extract HTTP calls into data/api/<feature>_api_service.dart
- [ ] Create abstract interface in domain/repositories/i_<feature>_repository.dart
- [ ] Create implementation in data/repositories/<feature>_repository.dart implementing the interface
- [ ] Move notifier to presentation/providers/<feature>_provider.dart
  - [ ] Change keepAlive: true → @riverpod
  - [ ] Notifier depends on interface, not concrete class
  - [ ] Convert synchronous TState pattern → AsyncValue<T> with build() returning Future
- [ ] Create all index.dart barrel files
- [ ] Check if models are shared (>3 files import them) → re-export, don't move
- [ ] Update all import sites to new path
- [ ] Run dart run build_runner build
- [ ] Run flutter analyze — fix all errors AND warnings (directives_ordering)
- [ ] Delete old lib/providers/<feature>.dart and <feature>.g.dart
- [ ] Run flutter analyze again to confirm no broken references

